The IRQ/mret run is hitting the important bins (`trap:irq`, CSR reads in handler, and `mret`) before the core redirects into unknown instruction data. Since the goal is functional coverage stimulus, I’m changing only the TB stop condition for that directed run to finish immediately after observing `mret`, keeping the measured bins and avoiding post-mret X pollution.
